--- Block 4 x=78.0..552.7 y=104.1..118.0 ---
Defined Approach Requirements 
Defined Approach Testing Procedures 
Purpose

--- Block 10 x=78.0..274.8 y=127.4..162.7 ---
11.4.4 Exploitable vulnerabilities and security 
weaknesses found during penetration testing are 
corrected as follows:

--- Block 13 x=298.2..502.9 y=127.4..174.1 ---
11.4.4 Examine penetration testing results to verify 
that noted exploitable vulnerabilities and security 
weaknesses were corrected in accordance with all 
elements specified in this requirement.

--- Block 11 x=78.0..288.6 y=164.8..199.7 ---
• 
In accordance with the entity’s assessment of 
the risk posed by the security issue as defined in 
Requirement 6.3.1.

--- Block 5 x=514.2..713.4 y=119.6..223.0 ---
The results of a penetration test are usually a 
prioritized list of vulnerabilities discovered by the 
exercise. Often a tester will have chained a 
number of vulnerabilities together to compromise 
a system component. Remediating the 
vulnerabilities found by a penetration test 
significantly reduces the probability that the same 
vulnerabilities will be exploited by a malicious 
attacker.

--- Block 12 x=78.0..266.0 y=201.8..225.5 ---
• 
Penetration testing is repeated to verify the 
corrections.

--- Block 14 x=78.0..226.8 y=235.7..249.3 ---
Customized Approach Objective

--- Block 15 x=78.0..287.7 y=259.2..282.9 ---
Vulnerabilities and security weaknesses found while 
verifying system defenses are mitigated.

--- Block 6 x=514.2..709.4 y=225.1..282.9 ---
Using the entity’s own vulnerability risk 
assessment process (see requirement 6.3.1) 
ensures that the vulnerabilities that pose the 
highest risk to the entity will be remediated more 
quickly.

--- Block 7 x=514.2..577.8 y=284.9..297.8 ---
Good Practice

--- Block 8 x=514.2..712.9 y=299.4..345.8 ---
As part of the entity’s assessment of risk, entities 
should consider how likely the vulnerability is to 
be exploited and whether there are other controls 
present in the environment to reduce the risk.

--- Block 9 x=514.2..714.8 y=347.9..371.6 ---
Any weaknesses that point to PCI DSS 
requirements not being met should be addressed.

--- Block 2 x=72.0..722.5 y=541.9..576.6 ---
